.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-git-clone 1  "snip 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
snip\-git\-clone \- Clone a snip library from a Git remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip git clone\fR [\fB\-\-gh\fR] [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-set\-default\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREMOTE\fR> [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clone a snip library from a Git remote
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-gh\fR
Clone with `gh repo clone` instead of `git clone`, so GitHub credentials come from the GitHub CLI
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-default\fR
Record the clone as default_library in the snip config
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREMOTE\fR>
Remote to clone. Passed to git unchanged; with \-\-gh it is passed to gh, which also accepts an OWNER/REPO shorthand
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Destination directory. Defaults to ~/<repo name>.sniplib
